ng industrial heritage, which is still present with companies such as the Volvo, as well as Scandinavia's largest port. The city hosts numerous national and international sporting and music events such as Gothia Cup, Partille Cup and Way Out West. Gothenburg is also home to the largest amusement park in the Nordics, Liseberg.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Gothenburg","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Gothenburg","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Gothenburg is a coastal city in Sweden with a strong food scene. Liseberg and the Gothenburg Cathedral stand out among about seventeen hours of touring, and the Museum of World Culture sits nearby, across June, July and August.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":608462,"visit_h":16.8}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-liseberg","name":"Liseberg","kind":"Theme park","lat":57.69556,"lon":11.99,"dist_km":1.8,"rank_score":11.13,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Liseberg%2C_20221223.jpg/960px-Liseberg%2C_20221223.jpg","author":"AleWi","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liseberg,_20221223.jpg","w":4080,"h":3072,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-ullevi","name":"Ullevi","kind":"Landmark","lat":57.70583,"lon":11.98722,"dist_km":1.2,"rank_score":9.83,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Ullevi_stadium_in_gothenburg_20060510.jpg/960px-Ullevi_stadium_in_gothenburg_20060510.jpg","author":"Martin Olsson (mnemo on en/sv wikipedia and commons, martin@minimum.se)","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ullevi_stadium_in_gothenburg_20060510.jpg","w":3038,"h":1049,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-gothenburg-museum-of-art","name":"Gothenburg Museum of Art","kind":"Museum","lat":57.69639,"lon":11.98056,"dist_km":